Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?OrionLayer=20Open=20Fix=2093:=20the=20LAYOUT=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?message=20=E2=80=94=20every=20member=20of=20the=20records=20the?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20wire=20sends=20raw,=20by=20name,=20offset=20and=20size?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The snapshot carries the game's records as raw bytes (s_player, s_colony, ...).
A client that reads fixed offsets breaks whenever a record changes: v2.0.0
grew s_player from 3,854 to 11,654 bytes. Right after HELLO_REPLY (whose
second word now carries CAP_LAYOUT, 0x0001) the server sends LAYOUT (0x15):
per record its name and size, per member its name, offset, size, element
size and kind; then MAX_PLAYERS, MAX_LEADERS, MAX_STARS, MAX_SHIPS,
MAX_PLANETS, MAX_NEBULAS. A client finds every member by name, so a record
that grows or moves needs no change on either side.

src/ext/ext_layout_table.inc lists the members; tools/ext_layout_gen.py
writes it from src/game/orion2.h (--check says whether it is current); the
offsets and sizes in it are the compiler's (offsetof, sizeof). A member that
is removed or renamed stops the build at its line. One module (ext_layout),
one hook (HELLO); the game's own structures and logic are untouched; built
only with ORION2RE_EXT. Documented in docs/extension-api.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
